Maintainer action required: this patch cannot be landed by the autonomous agent.

Why: .github/workflows/** is maintainer-managed. The repository-scoped GitHub App
token (ghs_*) has no `workflows` permission, so `git push` of a workflow change
is rejected, and .github/scripts/kilo-controller.sh restores .github/workflows from
origin/main after every session (and excludes those paths from staging). Committing
this change in-tree therefore does not persist; origin/main keeps the failing gates.yml.

Apply (maintainer, with workflow scope):
  git apply patches/0001-gates-workflow-contract-fix.patch
  git commit -am "fix(ci): satisfy gates workflow contract"
  git push origin main

What it changes in .github/workflows/gates.yml (the only file touched):
  - add 'scripts/**' to the push and pull_request path filters;
  - add `python -m pip install -e . --no-deps` to both jobs;
  - add `scripts` to both ruff targets;
  - add the backtest performance regression gate step to research_gates.

Verification (re-run with `python scripts/verify_gates_workflow_patch.py`):
  the patch applies cleanly to the live gates.yml and resolves all 7 assertions
  pinned by tests/test_gates_workflow.py (7 failed -> 7 passed). The script never
  modifies the working tree; it applies the patch to a throwaway copy. Re-verify
  after any change to gates.yml or the contract test.

